    "content": "St. John's University is a private Roman Catholic, Vincentian institution founded in 1870, based in Queens, NYC, with a focus on high-quality academics and service. Known as the Red Storm, the university has an ~83% acceptance rate, a 3.5 GPA average, and competitive men's basketball under coach Rick Pitino. Key Aspects of St. John's University (NY) Campuses: Main campus in Queens, with additional NY locations in Staten Island and Manhattan, plus international locations in Rome, Paris, and Seville. Academics: Offers a diverse range of undergraduate and graduate programs, emphasizing liberal arts, business, and professional studies. Admissions: The university is moderately selective, with a 2024 acceptance rate of 83.43% and admitted students typically having a GPA of around 3.5. Admissions Data: Half of the admitted applicants submit SAT scores between 1150 and 1340, or ACT scores between 24 and 29. Athletics: Competes in NCAA Division I as part of the Big East Conference, famously known for its basketball team. Note: The search results also contained information for distinct institutions like St. John's College at Oxford and St. John's College at UBC, which are not the same as St. John's University in New York.",
